msgid "\n\n[color=#8f8676]1919 年 11 月 6 日公布的結果：Sobral 1.98″、普林西比 1.61″，都比較接近愛因斯坦的 1.75″。怎麼得出、留下哪些疑問，見「歷史上發生了什麼」。[/color]"
msgstr "\n\n[color=#8f8676]Results announced on 6 November 1919: Sobral 1.98″, Príncipe 1.61″, both closer to Einstein's 1.75″. How they were obtained, and what doubts remained, are in 'What Happened Historically'.[/color]"

msgid "\n\n（"
msgstr ""

msgid "\n1919 年你改成：%s。"
msgstr "\nIn 1919 you changed it to: %s."

msgid "\nCottingham 只能自己趕著上發條，來不及對時。"
msgstr "\nCottingham had to wind the drive in haste, with no time to check the timing."

msgid "\n[b]歷史上[/b] [color=#8f8676](HISTORICAL_RECORD，詳見 docs/PROVENANCE.md)[/color]"
msgstr "\n[b]Historically[/b] [color=#8f8676](HISTORICAL_RECORD; see docs/PROVENANCE.md)[/color]"

msgid "\n[color=#8f8676][font_size=%d]虛構與示意：玩家角色、全部對白、時鐘驅動需要協助的情節、雲的細節、底片影像與所有數值。場景為推測重建；普林西比站沒有已知的現場照片，原始底片也已佚失。[/font_size][/color]"
msgstr "\n[color=#8f8676][font_size=%d]Fiction and illustration: the player character, all dialogue, the business of the clock drive needing help, the details of the cloud, the plate images and every figure. The scene is a speculative reconstruction; no photograph of the Príncipe station is known, and the original plates are lost.[/font_size][/color]"

msgid "\n[color=#fd8]合併：%.2f″ ± %.2f″（兩倍誤差 %.2f–%.2f″）[/color]"
msgstr "\n[color=#fd8]Combined: %.2f″ ± %.2f″ (twice the error: %.2f–%.2f″)[/color]"

msgid "\n你：『停！』　Eddington 換片——真的換片要四秒左右，這段時間按了也沒用。第三接觸之前一定要喊停。"
msgstr "\nYou: 'Stop!'  Eddington changes the plate—a real change takes about four seconds, and pressing during it does nothing. You must call stop before third contact."

msgid "\n全食時：空白鍵（或 RB／X）喊開始與停。"
msgstr "\nDuring totality: Space (or RB/X) calls start and stop."

msgid "\n快門還開著——最後那張底片曝到了陽光。"
msgstr "\nThe shutter is still open—the last plate caught the sunlight."

msgid "\n按「閃爍比對」：同一顆星，在兩張底片上跳一下——那一跳就是要量的東西。\n位移已放大，方便肉眼看見；真正的量測用顯微測微器。"
msgstr "\nPress 'Blink comparison': the same star jumps between the two plates—that jump is what you are measuring.\nThe displacement is exaggerated so the eye can see it; the real measurement uses the micrometer."

msgid "\n發條上滿了，但走速沒有校過。"
msgstr "\nThe drive is fully wound, but its rate was never checked."

msgid "\n第%d號還沒讀數，不會算進去。"
msgstr "\nPlate %d has no reading yet and will not be counted."

msgid "\n第一次量：%.2f″ ± %.2f″"
msgstr "\nFirst measurement: %.2f″ ± %.2f″"

msgid "\n第一次量：沒有量出任何數值。"
msgstr "\nFirst measurement: no value came out."

msgid "\n細線是兩倍誤差：Eddington 的判準是，兩倍誤差之內容得下哪個預測、又排除了哪個。"
msgstr "\nThe thin lines mark twice the error: Eddington's test is which prediction that range includes, and which one it excludes."

msgid "\n（和你的底片放在一起看——兩套儀器、隔一個大西洋。）"
msgstr "\n(Seen beside your plates—two instruments, an ocean apart.)"

msgid " ✓讀"
msgstr " ✓read"

msgid " 已記"
msgstr " noted"

msgid " 開始］"
msgstr ""

msgid "%.2f″ ± %.2f″（量 %d 張）"
msgid_plural "%.2f″ ± %.2f″（量 %d 張）"
msgstr[0] "%.2f″ ± %.2f″ (plates: %d)"
msgstr[1] "%.2f″ ± %.2f″ (plates: %d)"

msgid "%.2f″ ± %.2f″，兩倍誤差是 %.2f″ 到 %.2f″"
msgstr "%.2f″ ± %.2f″, twice the error spans %.2f″ to %.2f″"

msgid "%s\n\n（史實）"
msgstr "%s\n\n(Historical)"

msgid "%s\n\n（虛構）"
msgstr "%s\n\n(Fiction)"

msgid "%s 協助 Cottingham 上發條"
msgstr "%s Help Cottingham wind the drive"

msgid "%s 向 Eddington 報到"
msgstr "%s Report to Eddington"

msgid "%s 和 %s"
msgstr "%s and %s"

msgid "%s 從暗房（鐵皮屋頂的木屋）搬底片匣到望遠鏡架（已放 %d／%d，手上 %d）"
msgstr "%s Carry plate holders from the darkroom (the tin-roofed hut) to the telescope rack (set %d/%d, in hand %d)"

msgid "%s 用天文鐘替他校走速"
msgstr "%s Check his drive rate against the chronometer"

msgid "%s、%s 和 %s"
msgstr "%s, %s and %s"

msgid "%s。%s。"
msgstr "%s. %s."

msgid "%s。還有你。——14 號？讓我看看。"
msgstr "%s. And you.—Plate 14? Let me see."

msgid "%s九點前要 14 號星場的抄錄圖。說是「核對一下就好」。"
msgstr "%s wants the tracing of star field 14 before nine. Says it 'just needs checking'."

msgid "%s也對過一次吧？我看見紙上有兩種鉛筆的痕跡。寫上去。"
msgstr "%s checked it once too, didn't you? I can see two kinds of pencil on the sheet. Write that in."

msgid "%s大概跟你說過 Dyson 的那篇短文了。"
msgstr "%s has probably told you about Dyson's short paper."

msgid "%s我要說的只有一句：做他的清單，就像做我的一樣。哪顆星對不上，就寫它對不上。不管那對誰有利。"
msgstr "%s, I have only one thing to say: do his list as you would do mine. If a star doesn't match, write that it doesn't match. Whoever it favours."

msgid "%s的帳簿"
msgstr "%s's Ledger"

msgid "%s這回，你想改哪一步？先記住自己的打算。"
msgstr "%s This time, which step do you want to change? Remember your intention first."

msgid "%s（%s）"
msgstr "%s (%s)"

msgid "%s：%s"
msgstr "%s: %s"

msgid "+0.5°　E"
msgstr "+0.5°  E"

msgid "0.87″ 和 1.75″ 都不在範圍裡"
msgstr "Neither 0.87″ nor 1.75″ is inside the range"

msgid "0.87。牛頓式的算法給的就是這個。寫下來，比記在心裡好。"
msgstr "0.87. That is what the Newtonian calculation gives. Better written down than kept in the head."

msgid "0.87：照牛頓的算法，只有一半"
msgstr "0.87: half, on the Newtonian calculation"

msgid "1.75。愛因斯坦的全部。好——日食那天，我們看看底片怎麼說。"
msgstr "1.75. Einstein's full value. Good—on the day of the eclipse, we shall see what the plates say."

msgid "1.75：愛因斯坦的全部"
msgstr "1.75: Einstein's full value"

msgid "11 月 6 日，倫敦開會。"
msgstr "6 November: the meeting in London."

msgid "14 號星場　／　玻璃與描圖紙"
msgstr "Star field 14  /  glass and tracing paper"

msgid "17 個點重合了，還有 1 個沒有對上。也看看角落的編號，和鉛筆畫的箭頭。"
msgstr "17 points coincide; one still does not. Look also at the numbers in the corner, and the pencil arrows."

msgid "1846 年：Le Verrier 只用紙筆，算出一顆沒人見過的行星該在哪裡。Galle 當晚去找——離算出的位置不到一度。"
msgstr "1846: With nothing but pen and paper, Le Verrier calculated where a planet no one had seen ought to be. Galle looked that very night—less than a degree from the predicted position."

msgid "1910 年：哈雷彗星回來了。七十多年前就照牛頓的算法排好日子——Cowell 和 Crommelin 在彗星被望遠鏡再看見之前算的近日點（彗星最靠近太陽的那一刻），只早了不到三天。"
msgstr "1910: Halley's Comet returned. Its return had been dated more than seventy years before, using Newton's methods—Cowell and Crommelin's calculation of perihelion (the moment when the comet is closest to the Sun), made before the comet was sighted again through a telescope, was less than three days early."

msgid "1915 年 11 月，愛因斯坦說他的理論算得出水星那 43 角秒。消息傳到劍橋時，我想：先知道答案再去算，誰都算得對。"
msgstr "In November 1915, Einstein said his theory could account for Mercury's 43 arcseconds. When the news reached Cambridge, I thought: know the answer first, then calculate, and anyone can be right."

msgid "1915 年觀測日誌"
msgstr "Observing Log, 1915"

msgid "1917 年 11 月 10 日，聯合常設日食委員會決定：如果可能，派隊到巴西的 Sobral 和非洲西岸外海的普林西比島。"
msgstr "10 November 1917: the Joint Permanent Eclipse Committee resolves that, if possible, parties be sent to Sobral in Brazil and to the island of Príncipe off the west coast of Africa."

msgid "1917 年的帳本"
msgstr "The 1917 ledger"

msgid "1917 年的筆記"
msgstr "The 1917 notes"

msgid "1918 年 11 月，停戰。"
msgstr "November 1918. The Armistice."

msgid "1919 年 1 月，用[b]同一具望遠鏡[/b]在牛津夜空拍下的同一片星場（金牛座畢宿星團一帶）。日食這天，太陽正好在這片星前面。"
msgstr "January 1919: the same field, photographed at night over Oxford with [b]the same telescope[/b] (the region of the Hyades in Taurus). On the day of the eclipse the Sun stands in front of this field."

msgid "1919 年 11 月 6 日，皇家學會與皇家天文學會聯席會議公布結果。報告最倚重的是巴西 Sobral 的 4 吋望遠鏡（1.98″ ± 0.12″）；普林西比是 1.61″ ± 0.30″（當年寫的是「機率誤差」，約是一倍標準誤差的三分之二）。Sobral 天體照相儀的結果因焦距改變、星像模糊而未採用——這是有紀錄的技術理由，而非掩蓋。一次遠征並沒有讓所有疑問就此消失。"
msgstr "On 6 November 1919, the results were announced at a joint meeting of the Royal Society and the Royal Astronomical Society. The report relied chiefly on the 4-inch telescope at Sobral in Brazil (1.98″ ± 0.12″); Príncipe gave 1.61″ ± 0.30″ (written at the time as 'probable error', roughly two-thirds of one standard error). The Sobral astrographic result was set aside because the focal length had changed and the star images were blurred—a documented technical reason, not a cover-up. One expedition did not make every doubt disappear."

msgid "1919 年 3 月 8 日，兩支日食隊從利物浦搭船出發。"
msgstr "8 March 1919: the two eclipse expeditions sail from Liverpool."

msgid "1919 年 5 月 29 日"
msgstr "29 May 1919"

msgid "1919 年 5 月 29 日・普林西比"
msgstr "29 May 1919 · Príncipe"

msgid "1919 年 5 月 29 日有一次日全食。那天，太陽會停在金牛座一片星場的前面——那裡的亮星，多得不尋常。"
msgstr "There is a total eclipse of the Sun on 29 May 1919. That day the Sun will stand in front of a field of stars in Taurus—unusually rich in bright stars."

msgid "1979 年，有人重新量了 Sobral 的底片（Harvey）：4 吋 1.90″ ± 0.11″，天體照相儀 1.55″ ± 0.34″——支持了當年團隊對那組 0.93″ 的疑慮。"
msgstr "In 1979 the Sobral plates were measured again (Harvey): 4-inch 1.90″ ± 0.11″, astrographic 1.55″ ± 0.34″—supporting the team's doubts at the time about the 0.93″ set."

msgid "43 角秒很小：一度是 3600 角秒，它還不到一度的八十分之一。可是一百多年的紀錄量下來，這個差比量測誤差大得多，而且每個世紀都往同一邊多走，不會抵消。"
msgstr "43 arcseconds is very little: a degree is 3600 arcseconds, so it is less than an eightieth of a degree. But measurements from over a century of records put this discrepancy far beyond the errors of measurement. And the extra advance is in the same direction every century; it does not cancel out."

msgid "A 鍵"
msgstr "A button"

msgid "Ashby 先生"
msgstr "Mr Ashby"

msgid "Ashby 先生在走廊等你。"
msgstr "Mr Ashby is waiting for you in the corridor."

msgid "Ashby 先生寫的：0.87。\n你寫的：%s（%s）。"
msgstr "Ashby wrote: 0.87.\nYou wrote: %s (%s)."

msgid "Ashby 先生給的放大鏡。"
msgstr "The magnifying glass Ashby gave you."

msgid "Cottingham 在定天鏡那裡。早上的濕氣讓時鐘驅動不太聽話，他需要一雙手。"
msgstr "Cottingham is at the coelostat. The morning damp has made the clock drive sulky; he needs a pair of hands."

msgid "Cottingham 看過的那幾張，都在雲後面；其餘的，我說不上來。」"
msgstr "The ones Cottingham saw were all behind cloud; the rest, I can't say.'"

msgid "Cottingham：「一半在雲裡，一半透了光。」"
msgstr "Cottingham: 'Half in cloud, half let the light through.'"

msgid "Cottingham：「二十秒了——驅動沒對過時，再久星像會拖長。」"
msgstr "Cottingham: 'Twenty seconds—and with the drive unchecked, any longer and the star images will trail.'"

msgid "Cottingham：「二十秒了。」"
msgstr "Cottingham: 'Twenty seconds.'"

msgid "Cottingham：「太短了，大概什麼都沒留下。」"
msgstr "Cottingham: 'Too short. Probably nothing was caught.'"

msgid "Cottingham：「好，接著去天文鐘那裡。」"
msgstr "Cottingham: 'Good, then on to the chronometer.'"

msgid "Cottingham：「整段幾乎都在雲後面。」"
msgstr "Cottingham: 'Almost the whole of it was behind cloud.'"

msgid "Cottingham：「這幾秒雲很薄，我看得見日冕的邊。」"
msgstr "Cottingham: 'The cloud was thin for those seconds; I could see the edge of the corona.'"

msgid "Dyson 先生正有這個打算。一處下雨，另一處也許是晴天。"
msgstr "Sir Frank intends exactly that. If it rains at one, it may be clear at the other."

msgid "Dyson 的信（推測重建，非原文）"
msgstr "Dyson's letter (speculative reconstruction, not a quotation)"

msgid "Dyson、Eddington、Cottingham 與 1919 年的日食遠征為史實；你、Kit、Ashby 先生、劍橋的那一夜與所有對白為虛構，場景為推測重建。"
msgstr "Dyson, Eddington, Cottingham and the 1919 eclipse expedition are historical; you, Kit, Mr Ashby, that night in Cambridge and all dialogue are fiction, and the scenes are a speculative reconstruction."

msgid "Eddington 前幾天問我，這棟樓裡誰的紀錄最乾淨。"
msgstr "Eddington asked me the other day who in this building keeps the cleanest records."

msgid "Eddington 抬頭看了一眼：「雲還是很厚……繼續。」"
msgstr "Eddington glances up: 'The cloud is still thick… carry on.'"

msgid "Eddington 用手蓋住了這一格。"
msgstr "Eddington covers this panel with his hand."

msgid "Eddington 的清單。（把茶杯推過來，已經涼了）恭喜。真的。"
msgstr "Eddington's list. (Pushes a cup of tea across; it has gone cold.) Congratulations. Truly."

msgid "Eddington 還在換片……"
msgstr "Eddington is still changing the plate…"

msgid "Eddington 那個箱子，我後來又想了一次。這回在一面牆上開個小洞，讓一道光照進去。"
msgstr "I thought about Eddington's box again. This time, a small hole in one wall, with a beam of light let in."

msgid "Eddington："
msgstr "Eddington: "

msgid "Eddington：「最後一張了。」"
msgstr "Eddington: 'Last plate.'"

msgid "Eddington：「看太陽周圍那一小片，不是整片天。那裡變薄了就喊。」"
msgstr "Eddington: 'Watch that small patch around the Sun, not the whole sky. Call it when the cloud thins there.'"

msgid "Eddington：「還有 %d 張底片。」"
msgid_plural "Eddington：「還有 %d 張底片。」"
msgstr[0] "Eddington: \"%d plate left.\""
msgstr[1] "Eddington: \"%d plates left.\""

msgid "Eddington：沒有底片，只練眼睛和口令。看太陽那一塊雲——變薄就按［%s］喊『開始』，變厚之前喊『停』。"
msgstr "Eddington: No plates—we practise the eye and the calls only. Watch the cloud over the sun: when it thins, press [%s] and call 'start'; before it thickens, call 'stop'."

msgid "Greenwich 來信了。Dyson 寫的，在桌上。你先看。"
msgstr "A letter has come from Greenwich. It's from Dyson—on the table. You read it first."

msgid "Hall 試過：指數不是 2，是 2.00000016。水星對了——可是別的行星也得跟著對，這才是難處。"
msgstr "Hall tried it: the exponent is not 2 but 2.00000016. Mercury came out right—but the other planets have to come out right as well, and that is the difficulty."

msgid "KIT 的變星底片"
msgstr "KIT'S VARIABLE-STAR PLATES"

msgid "Kit 念出："
msgstr ""

msgid "Kit 念出：%s"
msgstr "Kit reads: %s"

msgid "Kit 念出：……"
msgstr "Kit reads: …"

msgid "LB／RB"
msgstr "LB/RB"

msgid "Le Verrier 也這麼想。日食的時候大家都在找它——1878 年有人說看見了，沒人能再看見一次。"
msgstr "Le Verrier thought so too. At eclipses everyone was looking for it—in 1878 someone claimed to have seen it, and no one ever saw it again."

msgid "Q　−0.5°"
msgstr "Q  −0.5°"

msgid "Q／E"
msgstr "Q/E"

msgid "RB／X 鍵"
msgstr "RB/X button"

msgid "Roça Sundy。莊園主人 Jerónimo Carneiro 讓遠征隊自由調用莊園的人手。挑夫把箱子扛過樹林，砌石墩、搭棚子時，莊園的人幫了大半的忙。報告裡沒有他們的名字。"
msgstr "Roça Sundy. The owner, Jerónimo Carneiro, let the expedition draw freely on the plantation's labour. Carriers brought the crates through the forest, and the plantation's people did most of the work on the stone pier and the huts. Their names are not in the report."

msgid "Seeliger 想過：太陽附近也許有一層看不見的物質，像黃道光的塵。聽起來很合理——可是沒有人能證明它多到足以拉住水星。"
msgstr "Seeliger considered it: perhaps there is unseen matter near the Sun, like the dust of the zodiacal light. It sounds reasonable—but no one could show there was enough of it to hold Mercury back."

msgid "Sobral 4 吋"
msgstr "Sobral 4-inch"

msgid "Sobral 4 吋那一點：細線（兩倍誤差）裡容得下哪一個？"
msgstr "The Sobral 4-inch point: which prediction falls within the thin line (twice the error)?"

msgid "Sobral 4 吋：1.98″，±0.12″ 機率誤差，約 0.18″ 標準差"
msgstr "Sobral 4-inch: 1.98″, ±0.12″ probable error, about 0.18″ standard deviation"

msgid "Sobral 天體照相儀"
msgstr "Sobral astrographic"

msgid "Sobral 天體照相儀：約 0.93″，沒有可靠的誤差"
msgstr "Sobral astrographic: about 0.93″, no reliable error"

msgid "Sobral 的 4 吋鏡頭"
msgstr "Sobral's 4-inch lens"

msgid "Sobral 的底片在 Greenwich 量完了。\n4 吋鏡頭：1.98″ ± 0.12″。\n天體照相儀：約 0.93″；星像模糊，當天的焦距和比例尺可能變了。"
msgstr "The Sobral plates have been measured at Greenwich.\n4-inch lens: 1.98″ ± 0.12″.\nAstrographic telescope: about 0.93″; the star images are blurred, and the focal length and plate scale may have changed that day."

msgid "WASD／左搖桿 移動 · 滑鼠／方向鍵／右搖桿 觀看 · Shift／L3 跑\n%s 互動 · %s 紀錄 · %s 開始與停 · %s 暫停"
msgstr "WASD/left stick move · mouse/arrows/right stick look · Shift/L3 run\n%s interact · %s log · %s start/stop · %s pause"

msgid "[b]Eddington 的回應[/b]"
msgstr "[b]Eddington's Reply[/b]"

msgid "[b]Godot 第三方元件[/b]"
msgstr "[b]Godot third-party components[/b]"

msgid "[b]Godot 第三方授權全文[/b]"
msgstr "[b]Godot third-party licence texts[/b]"

msgid "[b]你留下的證據[/b]"
msgstr "[b]The Evidence You Left[/b]"

msgid "[b]全食[/b]　[font_size=%d][color=#e88]%d[/color][/font_size] 秒"
msgstr "[b]Totality[/b]  [font_size=%d][color=#e88]%d[/color][/font_size] s"

msgid "[b]全食[/b]　剩餘 %d 秒（共 302）"
msgstr "[b]Totality[/b]  %d s left (of 302)"

msgid "[b]劍橋・1917[/b]\n%s\n[color=#b8ad98]看片台 · 觀測日誌 · %s · 筆記本\n%s 對話紀錄[/color]"
msgstr "[b]Cambridge · 1917[/b]\n%s\n[color=#b8ad98]Viewing table · observing log · %s · notebook\n%s dialogue log[/color]"

msgid "[b]劍橋・1917[/b]\n查看太陽系儀"
msgstr "[b]Cambridge · 1917[/b]\nLook at the orrery"

